:R-HSA-6799990  a           obo:GO_0008150 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Metals are necessary for all forms of life including microorganisms, evidenced by the fact that metal cations are constituents of approximately 40% of all proteins crystallized to date (Waldron KJ et al. 2009; Foster AW et al. 2014; Guengerich FP 2014, 2015). The ability of microorganisms to maintain the intracellular metal quota is essential and allows microorganisms to adapt to a variety of environments. Accordingly, the ability of the host to control metal quota at inflammation sites can influence host-pathogen interactions. The host may restrict microbial growth either by excluding essential metals from the microbes, by delivery of excess metals to cause toxicity, or by complexing metals in microorganisms (Becker KW & Skaar EP 2014)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Metal sequestration by antimicrobial proteins" ;
        dc:contributor      "Edited: Shamovsky, Veronica, 2016-08-15" , "Reviewed: Hains, David S, 2016-08-02" , "Authored: Shamovsky, Veronica, 2015-10-05" , "Reviewed: Jupe, Steve, 2016-04-15" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-6799990" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-6803157/R-HSA-6803157> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

